✗ handler imports a driver

    internal/modules/orders/application/place.go:3
      package example.com/fix/internal/modules/orders/application          (layer: application)
        imports github.com/MerseniBilel/warren/observability

  This is a wiring module, not an API:

      github.com/MerseniBilel/warren/observability

  installs the exporters and composes app.Traced and app.Metered around
  every route at BOOT (warren.md §7.1). A handler that imports it changes
  nothing about what it is instrumented with, and pays for the module's
  transitive dependencies in every build that names it.

  Fix one of:
    • A handler that needs a SPAN takes the tracer from OpenTelemetry's own
      global provider, which this module has already configured at boot.
      No Warren import is involved.
    • Correlation fields — trace_id, span_id, correlation_id — are already
      on log.FromContext(ctx). Log through it and they are there, with no
      import at all.
    • Everything else the module exposes is setup, and setup belongs in
      main.go.

1 violation(s) in 1 packages.

  Checked 1 feature module for cross-module imports.
